## 2. SOC Sensitivity (Same 22km route, varying start SOC)

| Start SOC | Final SOC | SOC Drop | Depleted? | Status |
|-----------|-----------|----------|-----------|--------|
| 100% | 99.41% | 0.59pp | No | 200 |
| 80% | 79.41% | 0.59pp | No | 200 |
| 50% | 49.41% | 0.59pp | No | 200 |
| 30% | 29.41% | 0.59pp | No | 200 |
| 20% | 19.41% | 0.59pp | No | 200 |
| 16% | 15.41% | 0.59pp | No | 200 |
| 10% | -- | -- | -- | **500** |

**Key Findings:**
- **SOC drop is perfectly constant at 0.59pp** regardless of starting SOC. This is **physically correct** -- FASTSim computes energy consumption based on the drive cycle, not the current SOC level. The absolute energy (kWh) used is the same; the percentage drop only changes when effective capacity changes (via SOH or temperature).
- **SOC=10% correctly triggers an error** -- the starting SOC (10%) is below the protection SOC (15%), so the system properly rejects this as unroutable.

